hello everyone i'm jesse i'm a  registered nurse and entrepreneur and i  make videos on minimalism and healthy  living  in this video i'm going to share with  you 50 things that i've declared from my  life  so that hopefully you can get some ideas  of things that you can declare in yours  to have a simpler happier life number  one  television yes you can survive without a  television  we got rid of our television because we  wanted to spend more time  together as a family and to have time  for our hobbies that we used to love  that were a bit more productive such as  my husband likes oil painting  i like to read we now have time for  those hobbies  and when somebody does come to visit us  the television is not the center focal  point we're not  just ignoring each other looking at a  screen we're actually talking we're  actually spending time together  number two netflix and hulu a lot of  these shows  we weren't even watching so they just  kind of were an extra expense at the end  of the month  and something else to think about having  to pay  number three and this one doesn't really  apply to me more so to my husband  but it was very difficult for him and it  was video games  number four is school awards and  certificates  matter of fact i actually took a  snapshot and downloaded my  bachelor's diploma and just got rid of  it completely  because it doesn't necessarily make me  proud  to say i have credentials what does  make me proud what does bring me joy is  to look at my family photos  to see the artwork that i have done or  that my husband has done  those things are more descriptive of who  i am as a person not a credential  number five is a vacuum this one is a  bit easier for my husband and i because  we just moved into our first home  and we have laminate flooring so no need  for a vacuum  number six might be surprising to some  of you and it is  my wedding dress our party favors  cards all of that wedding memorabilia  is that the word that you say i don't  really know but a lot of the  times i feel like we keep those things  locked up in an attic boxed up away for  nobody to use  and it's not the physical item  that has brought us joy it is the  closeness and unity in your relationship  as it is for us it didn't really mean  much to us to keep these items because  physical items can never replace the  intangible relationship that we have  number seven is souvenirs a lot of times  we find ourselves collecting these items  at places we visited and this special  stick  which we have no idea where it came from  but we remembered that we kept a special  stick from somewhere  only to just create more waste create  more expense  and we don't really need them number  eight is toaster and mini oven  i find that these bulkier items just  take up a lot more space  and the kitchen that we have now is a  bit small so i didn't want  these large items if i just want to bake  something and just put it in the oven or  my husband loves to build fires outside  so we just  cook outside a lot of the times and as  far as a toaster we just use a griddle  number nine is a dish rack i wanted to  do away with the dish rack because the  kitchen that we have  it again doesn't have a lot of counter  space so we didn't want things just  cluttering up the space i wanted it to  look open  and clean and i'm so fortunate that i  have a large farmhouse sink so i just  wash everything in there hand dry it and  put it away right away  it helps keep my kitchen clean and tidy  most of the time  most number 10 hair curlers  straighteners dryers  all of that equipment for hair i did  away with that about five years ago  because i started to not use them very  often they damaged my hair  and they just made my life more  complicated i don't feel like i really  need to do all that  number 11 i think is hard for a lot of  people and it is nail polish for mani  pedis  i currently don't own any nail polish i  hate the look of chipped nails and i'm  not about to paint my nails  every other day just to prevent that on  the occasion that i do have a special  event to where i need  to look a little bit more presentable as  far as my nails go i just borrow from my  sister borrow from a friend  number 12 is perfume perfume has  something called  endocrine disruptors which have been  linked to cancer  so i definitely opted out for that and i  just use essential oils as far as  smells number 13 is another toxic  and expensive item that i've cut out  from my life and it's lotions  creams body scrubs face washes all that  sort of personal care item  i use cast out soap beeswax balm and  coconut oil and that pretty much takes  care of all of my needs  and it's not toxic to my body number 14  is another on the toxic item list that  i've decluttered  and it is pads and tampons you'd be  surprised if you do your research on  just how harmful they can be  but i now just use a menstrual cup and  cloth pads  number 15 is statement jewelry i  actually now just own just a few pieces  of jewelry that i pretty much wear every  day  and then a few things here and there for  special occasions  number 16 gps i don't think that a lot  of us really need those anymore because  our cell phones already have them built  in  number 17 straws straws are harmful to  the environment well plastic straws are  but i just found that i don't even  really need the reusable straws either  so i just cut them out number 18 another  money saver  is ziploc bags i actually switched to a  silicone bag a couple of years ago and  i've just been using the same silicone  bags  washing them reusing them number 19  dish sponges i switched over to cloth  sponges because they're better for the  environment and i can just reuse them  and re-wash  number 20 pre-made mixes pancake mixes  cake mixes that sort of thing it  actually is pretty easy to make your own  bread and to make your own pancakes  cakes and that sort of stuff if you just  look up some recipes  you'd be surprised 2