ecause we do have  chickens and we do eat their eggs  but this is something that we no longer  spend in because it's better for our  health  and it's a lot better for the  environment and our wallet  31 disposable razors we no longer buy  these  if you want to look into that you can  use a safety razor or a rechargeable  electric razor  32 simple cookbooks pinterest does it  all  33 carbonated drinks we actually don't  ever really buy any carbonated drinks  again i have tea we have a water filter  and on the occasion that we want some  juice  i just use my juicer 34  wine glasses and flower vases i find  that good old mason jars do the trick 35  paper calendars i actually love that i  no longer use this i use a google  calendar  because i can share it with my husband i  can share it with my mom who takes care  of my child while i'm working  so i love it for that reason you can  share it with other people and you're  not  creating an extra item in your home  36 might be controversial to some people  but it's baby shoes  and first time really only one time  outfits  let's be real they wear it for like five  minutes and then they either fall off  or they get soiled 37  baby food makers and fancy baby gadgets  i have a whole list of ideas of things  that babies do not  need so if anybody's interested in that  particular list  let me know i could perhaps make a video  on that  38 and this might apply to people with  kids  is battery operated toys i found that a  lot of these items are flashy  they're over stimulating and i think  that they just rob children  of their own creativity 39  promotional t-shirts this one came about  from a documentary that we saw on the  harm  of the fashion industry so if we ever  have a fundraiser where they're asking  us  if we want to pay for a t-shirt we just  donate the money instead if we feel it  in our heart  number 40 manuals you don't really need  to keep a paper copy nowadays because  it's often easy to download them online  41. coffee maker or a kettle  we now just use instant coffee and we  use a pot if we want coffee or tea  42 a bit of a small item but let's be  real we don't need this lemon squeezers  and citrus squeezers  43 this one was painful for me and it  was  unused purses i had a collection of  different  brand name purses that i never used so  now i've limited myself to  one tote bag and one cross bag that's it  44 loofahs luffas you constantly use  you throw them away you get another one  you throw it away they create  so much waste and it's harmful for the  environment so we use a bamboo brush now  instead  45 shaving cream and defilatory creams  shaving cream i just find that soap  works for me i don't know  what you guys try and as far as  defilatory creams they're not very good  for you if you just smell them the  chemicals on them  should warn you 46.  this one was also painful for me and  it's gala style clothing or special  occasion clothing  a lot of the times i think we keep a  special item because  maybe someday i'll wear it or maybe  someday i'll fit into it  maybe someday and it just stays boxed up  stage box stuff  it's taking up space somebody else could  actually be using it  or you could perhaps sell it and make  some money out of it  47 is large unused gym equipment  by no means am i telling you to get rid  of this if you actually use this  and find value in these items but if you  have these items that you're not using  that are just collecting dust  then this is perhaps one way that you  can get a lot of  space in your home and perhaps the money  back  for me i had a treadmill in my house and  i realized  after a few months of having it that i  was going outside and jogging instead  i didn't really need a treadmill 48  tortilla maker this might not be very  applicable to many people  but for my husband and i we are mexican  so we felt that it was fitting we had a  tortilla maker  except through developing some more  health consciousness  we stopped making tortillas so we didn't  really need it anymore  49 is a grill we actually did have a  grill  but it broke and when it did i think it  was great  it couldn't have been better because my  husband started building fires outside  and it started to become more about the  experience of let's go out as a family  let's go find firewood and let's go prep  this fire and let's go  get all the ingredients together it  became more of like a picnic  event so it was great for us  number 50 is very special to me and it's  decorations and knickknacks that we  either  don't believe to be beautiful or to have  a special meaning  we are very intentional about the kinds  of items that we bring into our home  because we feel that home whether it's  an apartment a rental  a house it doesn't matter home should be  like  base when you're playing tag it should  feel like a safe place  open clean and inspiring  so everything that we own either has a  purpose or we find to be beautiful  your idea of what brings inspiration and  beauty is going to be different  but i hope that in any case this gives  you some ideas of things that you can  declutter  so that your space can be more inspiring  and feel more like you  a home free of clutter is the mind free  of clutter  i hope that you love this if you found  any of those tips to be helpful  please give me a like and a thumbs up  and you can comment down below  let me know which of these was the most  helpful for you  thank you bye  you

